{"name":"Wetland Clay","hex":"#c1a98f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wetland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Land that is covered mostly with water, with occasional marshy and soggy areas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wetland"},{"term":"clay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mineral substance made up of small crystals of silica and alumina, that is ductile when moist; the material of pre-fired ceramics.","An earth material with ductile qualities."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add clay to or to spread clay onto.","To purify using clay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wetland","blocks":[{"text":"A wetland is a distinct semi-aquatic ecosystem whose groundcovers are flooded or saturated in water, either permanently, for years or decades, or only seasonally. Flooding results in oxygen-poor (anoxic) processes taking place, especially in the soils. Wetlands form a transitional zone between waterbodies and dry lands, and are different from other terrestrial or aquatic ecosystems due to their vegetation's roots having adapted to oxygen-poor waterlogged soils. They are considered among the most biologically diverse of all ecosystems, serving as habitats to a wide range of aquatic and semi-aquatic plants and animals, with often improved water quality due to plant removal of excess nutrients such as nitrates and phosphorus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/330px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wetland","wikidata":"Q170321"},{"title":"Clay","blocks":[{"text":"Clay is a type of fine-grained natural soil material containing clay minerals. Most pure clay minerals are white or light-coloured, but natural clays show a variety of colours from impurities, such as a reddish or brownish colour from small amounts of iron oxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg/330px-Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clay","wikidata":"Q42302"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Freshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg/500px-Freshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Freshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg/1280px-Freshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Freshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg/500px-Freshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFreshwater_swamp_forest_in_Gowainghat_Sylhet_Bangladesh_photo_taken_in_July_2016.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tourbi%C3%A8re_03_-_Parc_de_Frontenac_-_Juillet_2008.jpg/500px-Tourbi%C3%A8re_03_-_Parc_de_Frontenac_-_Juillet_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tourbi%C3%A8re_03_-_Parc_de_Frontenac_-_Juillet_2008.jpg/1280px-Tourbi%C3%A8re_03_-_Parc_de_Frontenac_-_Juillet_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikim